\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{Relation to the parity index}
\date{2026-11-23}

\p{For [based cochains](fdip-00SH) over a field of
characteristic different from #{2}, \ref{fdip-00T0} computes
the even-to-odd block index of #{\extD_U} and #{\cov_U}:
##{\dim\ker B-\dim\operatorname{coker} B
=\dim C^{\mathrm{even}}-\dim C^{\mathrm{odd}},}
where #{B} is the corresponding even-to-odd block. Both full
operators are odd for cell parity. Their generalized kernels
have this same integer as their super-dimension by
\ref{fdip-013P}. On complex cochains with the positive counting
inner product, the operator #{\extd+\extdag} is self-adjoint,
so \ref{fdip-013Q} gives the same integer for its ordinary
kernel.}
